# Serverless Framework Development Rules

## Core Principles

- **Infrastructure as Code**: Define all AWS resources in serverless.yml
- **Environment Separation**: Use different stages for dev, staging, and production
- **Security First**: Implement least privilege access and secure defaults
- **Cost Optimization**: Monitor and optimize Lambda execution costs

## Project Structure

```
project/
├── serverless.yml              # Main serverless configuration
├── serverless/
│   ├── functions/             # Lambda function configurations
│   ├── resources/             # CloudFormation resources
│   └── plugins/               # Custom serverless plugins
├── src/                       # Source code
├── tests/                     # Test files
├── .env.{stage}              # Environment-specific variables
├── pnpm-lock.yaml            # pnpm lock file
└── package.json
```

## Serverless Configuration Rules

- **Stage Management**: Use environment variables for stage-specific configuration
- **Resource Naming**: Use consistent naming conventions with stage prefixes
- **Memory Allocation**: Optimize Lambda memory based on workload requirements
- **Timeout Settings**: Set appropriate timeouts for different function types

```yaml
service: dualinga-api
frameworkVersion: '3'

provider:
  name: aws
  runtime: nodejs22.x
  stage: ${opt:stage, 'dev'}
  region: ${opt:region, 'us-east-1'}
  memorySize: 512
  timeout: 30
  environment:
    NODE_ENV: ${self:provider.stage}
    STAGE: ${self:provider.stage}
    REGION: ${self:provider.region}
  iam:
    role:
      statements:
        - Effect: Allow
          Action:
            - dynamodb:*
          Resource:
            - 'arn:aws:dynamodb:${self:provider.region}:*:table/${self:service}-${self:provider.stage}-*'
        - Effect: Allow
          Action:
            - s3:*
          Resource:
            - 'arn:aws:s3:::${self:service}-${self:provider.stage}-*/*'

custom:
  stage: ${self:provider.stage}
  region: ${self:provider.region}
  tableName: ${self:service}-${self:provider.stage}-users
  bucketName: ${self:service}-${self:provider.stage}-assets
```

## Function Configuration Rules

- **Handler Paths**: Use consistent handler path structure
- **Environment Variables**: Pass only necessary environment variables to functions
- **VPC Configuration**: Configure VPC only when necessary for database access
- **Layers**: Use Lambda layers for shared dependencies

```yaml
functions:
  graphql:
    handler: src/handlers/graphql.handler
    events:
      - http:
          path: /graphql
          method: post
          cors: true
          authorizer: jwtAuthorizer
    environment:
      GRAPHQL_ENDPOINT: /graphql
      LOG_LEVEL: ${self:custom.logLevel}
    memorySize: 1024
    timeout: 30
    reservedConcurrency: 100

  userCreated:
    handler: src/handlers/user-created.handler
    events:
      - stream:
          arn: !GetAtt UsersTable.StreamArn
          batchSize: 10
          startingPosition: LATEST
    environment:
      SNS_TOPIC_ARN: !Ref UserCreatedTopic
    memorySize: 256
    timeout: 10

  scheduledTask:
    handler: src/handlers/scheduled-task.handler
    events:
      - schedule:
          rate: rate(1 hour)
          enabled: ${self:custom.enableScheduledTasks}
    environment:
      TASK_TYPE: hourly
    memorySize: 512
    timeout: 60
```

## Resource Management Rules

- **DynamoDB Tables**: Use on-demand billing for development, provisioned for production
- **S3 Buckets**: Enable versioning and lifecycle policies
- **API Gateway**: Use custom domain names and SSL certificates
- **CloudWatch**: Configure proper logging and monitoring

```yaml
resources:
  Resources:
    UsersTable:
      Type: AWS::DynamoDB::Table
      Properties:
        TableName: ${self:custom.tableName}
        BillingMode: ${self:custom.billingMode, 'PAY_PER_REQUEST'}
        AttributeDefinitions:
          - AttributeName: id
            AttributeType: S
          - AttributeName: email
            AttributeType: S
        KeySchema:
          - AttributeName: id
            KeyType: HASH
        GlobalSecondaryIndexes:
          - IndexName: EmailIndex
            KeySchema:
              - AttributeName: email
                KeyType: HASH
            Projection:
              ProjectionType: ALL
        TimeToLiveSpecification:
          AttributeName: ttl
          Enabled: true
        PointInTimeRecoverySpecification:
          PointInTimeRecoveryEnabled: true

    AssetsBucket:
      Type: AWS::S3::Bucket
      Properties:
        BucketName: ${self:custom.bucketName}
        VersioningConfiguration:
          Status: Enabled
        LifecycleConfiguration:
          Rules:
            - Id: DeleteOldVersions
              Status: Enabled
              NoncurrentVersionExpiration:
                NoncurrentDays: 30
        PublicAccessBlockConfiguration:
          BlockPublicAcls: true
          BlockPublicPolicy: true
          IgnorePublicAcls: true
          RestrictPublicBuckets: true
```

## Environment Management Rules

- **Stage Separation**: Use different serverless.yml files or stage-specific variables
- **Secrets Management**: Use AWS Secrets Manager for sensitive data
- **Environment Files**: Use .env files for local development only
- **Parameter Store**: Use SSM Parameter Store for configuration values

```yaml
custom:
  # Environment-specific configurations
  config:
    dev:
      logLevel: debug
      enableScheduledTasks: false
      billingMode: PAY_PER_REQUEST
      corsOrigin: http://localhost:3000
    staging:
      logLevel: info
      enableScheduledTasks: true
      billingMode: PROVISIONED
      corsOrigin: https://staging.dualinga.com
    prod:
      logLevel: warn
      enableScheduledTasks: true
      billingMode: PROVISIONED
      corsOrigin: https://dualinga.com

  # Use stage-specific configuration
  logLevel: ${self:custom.config.${self:provider.stage}.logLevel}
  enableScheduledTasks: ${self:custom.config.${self:provider.stage}.enableScheduledTasks}
  billingMode: ${self:custom.config.${self:provider.stage}.billingMode}
  corsOrigin: ${self:custom.config.${self:provider.stage}.corsOrigin}
```

## Deployment Rules

- **Staging Deployment**: Always deploy to staging before production
- **Rollback Strategy**: Implement automatic rollback on deployment failures
- **Blue-Green Deployment**: Use blue-green deployment for zero-downtime updates
- **Monitoring**: Monitor deployment metrics and function performance

```bash
# Development deployment
serverless deploy --stage dev --verbose

# Staging deployment
serverless deploy --stage staging --verbose

# Production deployment (with confirmation)
serverless deploy --stage prod --verbose --confirm

# Function-specific deployment
serverless deploy function --function graphql --stage prod

# Rollback to previous version
serverless rollback --stage prod
```

## Plugin Management Rules

- **Essential Plugins**: Use only necessary plugins to minimize deployment time
- **Plugin Updates**: Keep plugins updated to latest stable versions
- **Custom Plugins**: Create custom plugins only when necessary
- **Plugin Configuration**: Configure plugins with proper options

```yaml
plugins:
  - serverless-offline
  - serverless-dotenv-plugin
  - serverless-webpack
  - serverless-dynamodb-local

custom:
  webpack:
    webpackConfig: webpack.config.js
    includeModules: true
    excludeFiles: '**/*.test.ts'

  dotenv:
    path: .env.${self:provider.stage}
    basePath: .env

  offline:
    httpPort: 3000
    lambdaPort: 3002
    noPrependStageInUrl: true
```

## Testing & Quality Rules

- **Local Testing**: Use serverless-offline for local development and testing
- **Integration Testing**: Test functions with real AWS services in staging
- **Performance Testing**: Monitor Lambda cold start times and execution duration
- **Cost Monitoring**: Track and optimize Lambda execution costs

```yaml
custom:
  # Testing configuration
  test:
    coverage: true
    timeout: 10000
    environment: test

  # Performance monitoring
  monitoring:
    enableXRay: true
    logRetentionInDays: 14
    metrics: true

  # Cost optimization
  costOptimization:
    enableReservedConcurrency: true
    enableProvisionedConcurrency: false
    memoryOptimization: true
```

## Security Best Practices

- **IAM Roles**: Use least privilege principle for IAM roles
- **VPC Configuration**: Configure VPC only when necessary
- **Encryption**: Enable encryption at rest and in transit
- **Network Security**: Use security groups and NACLs appropriately

```yaml
provider:
  iam:
    role:
      statements:
        # DynamoDB access
        - Effect: Allow
          Action:
            - dynamodb:GetItem
            - dynamodb:PutItem
            - dynamodb:UpdateItem
            - dynamodb:DeleteItem
            - dynamodb:Query
            - dynamodb:Scan
          Resource:
            - 'arn:aws:dynamodb:${self:provider.region}:*:table/${self:custom.tableName}'
            - 'arn:aws:dynamodb:${self:provider.region}:*:table/${self:custom.tableName}/index/*'

        # S3 access
        - Effect: Allow
          Action:
            - s3:GetObject
            - s3:PutObject
            - s3:DeleteObject
          Resource:
            - 'arn:aws:s3:::${self:custom.bucketName}/*'

        # CloudWatch Logs
        - Effect: Allow
          Action:
            - logs:CreateLogGroup
            - logs:CreateLogStream
            - logs:PutLogEvents
          Resource: 'arn:aws:logs:${self:provider.region}:*:*'
```

## Monitoring & Logging Rules

- **CloudWatch Logs**: Configure proper log retention and filtering
- **X-Ray Tracing**: Enable X-Ray for distributed tracing
- **Custom Metrics**: Implement custom CloudWatch metrics for business logic
- **Alerts**: Set up CloudWatch alarms for critical metrics

```yaml
custom:
  # Logging configuration
  logging:
    level: ${self:custom.logLevel}
    retentionInDays: 14
    enableXRay: true

  # Monitoring and alerting
  monitoring:
    enableAlarms: true
    alarmEmail: ${self:custom.alarmEmail}
    criticalErrorsThreshold: 5
    highLatencyThreshold: 5000
```
